  "equipment_type": "General purpose I/O controller (Verasys)",
  "applies_to": "Verasys generic IO controllers with digital and analog inputs, outputs, NetSensors and energy meters on the system bus.",
  "summary": "The generic IO controller brings miscellaneous points into Verasys: four binary inputs, five analog inputs with alarm limits, nine outputs, up to five temperature/humidity and eight temperature/CO2 NetSensors with alarm limits, and up to four energy meters. Through the SBH it exposes 198 objects.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object names are the short Verasys names as printed. The guide gives no units or state texts; multistate state texts come from the device.",
    "Access is from the Writable column (TRUE = writable).",
    "Source: LIT-12013287 Table 8 'BACnet attributes' (198 objects)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Verasys BACnet over IP Integration User Guide",
    "doc_number": "LIT-12013287",
